Enhancement: Dump multiple paths into one archive

The dump command accepts multiple files and directories. It writes one archive
with paths relative to the selected snapshot root, preserving the existing
single-directory path layout. Overlapping selections are included once.
Use snapshotID:subfolder to select the archive root and --force-archive to
wrap a single file in an archive. A lone file still produces raw output by
default. Missing selections fail before archive output starts.

